{
  "info": {
    "name": "ArmourAPI Attack Corpus",
    "description": "Versioned attack corpus, one folder per threat-matrix row (doc Section 4.3), numbered to match that section. Execution order differs from the numbering: folder 3 (Brute Force & Credential Stuffing) runs LAST because it deliberately blocklists its own source IP, which would otherwise contaminate every later folder sharing that IP. Run against the \"protected\" environment (through ArmourAPI) to verify blocking; run the same payloads against the \"baseline\" environment (direct to each real target) once Docker/testbeds are available, and diff the two - that diff is the Validation Test Report deliverable (doc Section 6). Folders 1, 4, 5, and 6 include KNOWN GAP / NOTE comments where current coverage is partial or untested - do not report those as fully mitigated.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Setup",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Login (capture ArmourAPI session token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"login reachable\", function () { pm.response.to.not.be.error; });",
                  "const token = pm.response.headers.get('X-ArmourAPI-Access-Token');",
                  "if (token) { pm.environment.set('access_token', token); }",
                  "pm.test(\"access token issued\", function () { pm.expect(token).to.be.a('string'); });"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/auth/login",
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\"email\":\"attacker-corpus@test.com\",\"password\":\"whatever-upstream-accepts\"}",
              "options": {
                "raw": {
                  "language": "json"
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. BOLA-IDOR (API1:2023)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Sequential order ID enumeration - /orders/1042",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test(\"auth required and present -> not auth-rejected\", function () {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.body ? pm.response.json() : {};",
                  "  pm.expect(['auth-missing','auth-invalid','auth-revoked']).to.not.include(body.category);",
                  "});",
                  "// KNOWN GAP: ArmourAPI requires *a* valid token on this route (FR6) but does not",
                  "// verify the token's subject owns order 1042 (object-level ownership matching is",
                  "// not implemented - see Phase 7 notes). This request is expected to pass the",
                  "// gateway either way; true BOLA prevention would need to happen at the upstream",
                  "// or via an ownership-aware authorization layer not yet built."
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{access_token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": "{{base_url}}/api/v1/orders/1042"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
